// A2 course (A1 → A2 roadmap), module 7 „Pood, raha ja ostud” (a2-031…035), level A2. Lesson template v4
// (docs/COURSE_DESIGN_COMMUNICATIVE.md §12, docs/METHODOLOGY_STANDARD.md). One storyline, one year before the B1
// course (docs/COURSE_CAST.md): Sofia (27) rents a room from Malle Pärn in Mustamäe, flatmate Grete (22). It is late
// November, Sofia's first Estonian winter: she has only a thin autumn jacket. Goal, said on the first sheet: at the end
// the learner returns a broken thing at the shop counter with the receipt and writes a message comparing two offers
// (034 Kasuta, final project).
//   031 Kaubahall (department store) with Grete — clothes and colours, the partitive of adjective + noun (Ma otsin
//       sooja musta jopet, Mul on vaja sooje saapaid); a birthday present for Malle from the store's catalogue.
//   032 Nõmme market (Viktor's apples, eggs and honey; Leida's woollen socks and mittens) and the till — numbers and
//       prices; numbers in cases, the module's grammar item (A2 grammar plan: 07): kahe euro eest, viie euroga,
//       kaheksast kolmeni, kümne protsendi soodustus, kuni viiekümne euroni; the shared food basket of the flat, a
//       wrong receipt; a phone call about second-hand boots (agreeing a price).
//   033 the second-hand shop „Teine Ring” — the comparative (odavam, soojem … kui; Kas teil on suuremat?), a toy
//       penguin for Mia, choosing between three jackets.
//   034 the kettle that broke after ten days — kuni reedeni, … jooksul, kviitungiga / ilma kviitungita, tagastama,
//       vahetama; numbers in cases again (kahe aasta garantii, kella kümnest kuueni); Viktor goes along to the shop.
// Recycling of module 6 (food and café): leib, piim, juust, kohv, tee, supp, kilo, pakk, purk, muna, õun, mesi,
// kartul, maitsev, kohvik, sularaha. Harno A2 formats trained: short-answer listening (played twice), dialogue T/F,
// set phrases MC, signs matching, a letter with 3-option gaps, a ~150-word text, a message ≥ 30 words, picture
// description, role cards in pairs. Lesson 5 is the module's check (unchanged). The v3 file is in
// archive/v3/a2/module07.js.
